# Written by scripts/stack-up.sh — machine-local, never committed. It holds an API key and the
# addresses of a throwaway stack; it is regenerated by every run and meaningless five minutes after
# the stack is destroyed, but it is still a credential, and credentials do not go in git even when
# they are worthless.
.stack.json

# The default output paths of a run. A report worth keeping is committed under `reports/` with a
# dated, run-identified name, so runs accumulate and can be compared; these two are overwritten by
# every execution, and tracking them would turn each run into a meaningless diff of the last one.
simulation-report.md
simulation-report.json
